  "title": "Election Commission Bars Trinamool Factions from Using Party Symbols",
  "summary": "The Election Commission has barred both factions of the All India Trinamool Congress (AITC) from using their party name and symbol during the West Bengal bypolls. The Commission requested a substantive determination by the poll body under provisions of the Election Symbols (Reservatio) Order 1968.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Election Commission has barred both factions of the All India Trinamool Congress from using party name and symbol in West Bengal bypolls.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Commission directed the rival factions to submit preferred names and symbols by Friday morning.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Commission ruled that there are two rival groups in the AITC, one led by Mamata Banerjee and the other by Shri Arup Roy.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
